From: A23 maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] mm: complete the vmpressure accounting backport

This tree's vmpressure API also requires the allocation order. The backport
that moved subtree accounting before reclaimed_slab omitted that argument and
left the old call in place. Pass sc->order and account the subtree only once,
before adding slab pages whose scans are not included in nr_scanned.

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -5691,18 +5691,13 @@
 		 */
 		vmpressure(sc->gfp_mask, sc->target_mem_cgroup, true,
 			   sc->nr_scanned - nr_scanned,
-			   sc->nr_reclaimed - nr_reclaimed);
+			   sc->nr_reclaimed - nr_reclaimed, sc->order);
 
 		if (reclaim_state) {
 			sc->nr_reclaimed += reclaim_state->reclaimed_slab;
 			reclaim_state->reclaimed_slab = 0;
 		}
 
-		/* Record the subtree's reclaim efficiency */
-		vmpressure(sc->gfp_mask, sc->target_mem_cgroup, true,
-			   sc->nr_scanned - nr_scanned,
-			   sc->nr_reclaimed - nr_reclaimed, sc->order);
-
 		if (sc->nr_reclaimed - nr_reclaimed)
 			reclaimable = true;
 
